# ── secrets / credentials — NEVER publish ────────────────────────────────────
# The whole point of this SDK is handling credentials; none may ever land in git.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.crt
*.jks
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
token
tokens.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*_rsa
*_ed25519
.netrc

# ── internal / not for public consumption ────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC. Internal planning artefacts live in the private repos that
# consume this SDK, never here.
#
# pmm/ is the user-journey product review: buyer-lifecycle analysis, a candid
# register of every defect found with severities, and journeys written in terms of
# how we currently fail each kind of customer. All of it is accurate and useful
# INTERNALLY, and all of it reads as "here is everything wrong with our product"
# to anyone evaluating us. The findings belong in the fixes, which ship; the
# analysis that produced them does not.
#
# Deliberate call, not an oversight: the SOP (00) and the harness (03) would both
# be defensible public artefacts on their own, but splitting a numbered set is
# worse than keeping it whole. Revisit as a decision, not by accident.
pmm/
tickets/
ticket/
_internal/
_private/
*_INTERNAL.md
*_PRIVATE.md
scratch/
notes/
TODO.local.md

